57bm-i15"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i15"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i15","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.124 (A general perturbed greedy recurrence)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.124, p. 78, label record:257bm-i15","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let the old integer values be separated by at least $g\\ge1$, and let the update be $t(x)=4s(x)+p(x)$ with $0\\le p(x)\\le B<g$. Suppose $x_-$ and $x_+$ are the adjacent old values on either side of capacity $C$. Theorem 6.62 gives the largest admissible updated value at capacity $4C+g$ and the exact three-branch remainder after testing the extra weight $2g+4$.*\n\n*The underlying structure in Definition 6.61 assumes only $B<3g$; that suffices for order preservation, but the cited maximality application has the additional hypothesis $B<g$. The counterexample after Theorem 6.62 shows what can fail without it. For a maximum over both choices of the extra weight, rather than the stated two-stage rule, one also needs a separation argument; $4g-B\\ge2g+4$ suffices, as shown after that theorem.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-i15","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-i15","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i15%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_perturbed_nextRemainder_three_branches%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i15%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_perturbed_nextRemainder_three_branches%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e25